        {
          "type": "agentMessage",
          "id": "c6eac88e-ebb8-5890-a50d-cb246f812438",
          "text": "Agreed. **Assume cell \\(i\\) has already been selected.** Selection probabilities and scheduling are outside this discussion.\n\nFor its ordinary move, the proposal is:\n\n- Freeze densities: \\(\\widehat W_j(q)=\\rho_j A_j(q)\\).\n- Fix the scoring set \\(S_i=\\{i\\}\\cup N_i(0)\\).\n- Measure neighborhood imbalance by\n  \\[\n  E_i(q)=\\sum_{j\\in S_i}\\frac{1}{|N_j(q)|}\n  \\sum_{k\\in N_j(q)}\n  |\\widehat W_j(q)-\\widehat W_k(q)|.\n  \\]\n- **Balance move:** move only \\(i\\) in a direction that decreases \\(E_i\\).\n- **Circularity move:** improve \\(i\\)’s circularity without increasing \\(E_i\\).\n- Maintain the relevant condition along the move, staying inside the domain and avoiding collisions. Stop at the first adjacency change and refresh information.\n\nThe first question to settle is: **do we use this sum of local mean gaps as the balance objective for a single move?**"
